# Corpus unit rice/C01 — justified (the analytic-bound / consequence-check two-strand path)
#
# Source: m0/annotations/rice.yaml C01 (comparative, analytic_bound_with_consequence_check;
# corpus pin 62e9b54). Headline: RICE achieves a tighter sub-optimality bound via an
# explanation-guided mixed initial distribution — MaskNet-identified critical states give a
# smaller distribution-mismatch coefficient (linf norm) than the random-explanation baseline
# (Lemma 3.5, Theorem 3.6), yielding a tighter Theorem 3.6 bound; E03 checks the observable
# consequence (final reward) across 8 environments.
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * Two support strands (M0 summary section 3(a): rice C01 is a heterogeneous-support case).
#     Strand A is the analytic derivation (Lemma 3.5 / Theorem 3.6). Strand B is the E03
#     controlled comparison of final reward. They conclude DIFFERENT predicates
#     (holds_analytically vs better), so they cannot both conclude one claim formal; the
#     "two complete args to the same formal" option is unavailable. Strand B is also
#     incomplete at corpus-v1's bar (its significance/variance CQ is unmet-gap). So per the
#     "pick the binding strand and note the other" rule I take the ANALYTIC strand as binding:
#     the annotation scheme (analytic_bound_with_consequence_check) maps to analytic_argument,
#     and the claim title is explicitly about the bound.
#   * assumptions_hold is discharged from annotation CQ "Does Assumption 3.4 hold?" (met:
#     E01 fidelity of the optimized mask network significantly exceeds Random across 8 envs,
#     an empirical proxy the annotator rated met), together with Assumption 3.1.
#   * scope_licensed has no matching annotated CQ; discharged on the honest basis that
#     Theorem 3.6 / Lemma 3.5 derive the tighter bound for exactly the claimed mixed initial
#     distribution (Appendix B.2) — recorded here per the no-matching-CQ rule.
#   * Strand B and its gap are noted, not lowered: E03 reports mean and std over 3 seeds with
#     no significance test (annotation CQ3, mandatory unmet-gap), and the mismatch coefficient
#     is never measured directly (CQ4, optional unmet-gap). These bound the empirical
#     consequence-check strand, not the binding analytic derivation. The strict arithmetic
#     adapter for the derivation does not exist yet (policy design note); it lowers through the
#     defeasible analytic_argument until then.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact rice at sha256:1198f69a94a0
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim -------------------------------------------------------------------------

claim c01
  nl      = "RICE achieves a tighter sub-optimality bound via an explanation-guided mixed initial distribution: MaskNet-identified critical states give a smaller distribution mismatch coefficient (linf norm) than the random-explanation baseline (Lemma 3.5, Theorem 3.6), so the mixed-distribution bound is tighter; E03 checks the observable consequence (final reward) but reports no significance test"
  formal  = holds_analytically(rice_mixed_tighter_bound)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = unreviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Principal premise: the Lemma 3.5 / Theorem 3.6 derivation that MaskNet-guided initial sampling
# equals sampling from an improved policy, giving the smaller mismatch coefficient and tighter bound.
leaf e1 : derives(masknet_bound_derivation, rice_mixed_tighter_bound)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/claims.md#C01, Lemma-3-5, Theorem-3-6, Appendix-B-2, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N10]

# assumptions_hold: Assumption 3.1 (blinding cannot increase return) and Assumption 3.4 (mask
# confidence tracks state importance), the latter met via the E01 fidelity proxy (annotation CQ met).
leaf e2 : assumptions_established(masknet_bound_derivation)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [Assumption-3-1, Assumption-3-4, logic/experiments.md#E01]

# scope_licensed: Theorem 3.6 derives the tighter bound for exactly the claimed mixed initial
# distribution (no-matching-CQ honest basis).
leaf e3 : scope_licensed(rice_mixed_tighter_bound)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [Theorem-3-6, Appendix-B-2]

# --- The support argument (binding analytic strand) ---------------------------------------------

arg a1 : supports(c01) by analytic_argument(rice_mixed_tighter_bound, masknet_bound_derivation)
  discharge assumptions_hold with e2
  discharge scope_licensed   with e3

status c01

# ==============================================================================================
# EXPECTED VERDICT (golden oracle)
# ==============================================================================================
# Compiled AF: a1 alone, unattacked -> in (grounded).
# Claim status:
#   c01 -> justified (its complete support a1 is `in`; spec section 8 aggregation)
